      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Each side of an ice cube has length $\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{in}.$ What is the volume of the ice cube?",
      "worked_solution": "We need to find the volume of a cube.\n\nThe volume $V$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\nV={(\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{in})}^{3}=\\frac{1}{8}\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the ice cube is $\\frac{1}{8}\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.$",
